{"title":"Greenland fact of the day","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/940653626/0/marginalrevolution~Greenland-fact-of-the-day.html","date":1768834462000,"content":"<blockquote><p>Greenland held a referendum on <strong>23 February 1982</strong> and voted to <strong>leave the European Communities / European Economic Community (EEC)</strong> (about <strong>52–53%</strong> for leaving).</p></blockquote>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://chatgpt.com/share/696d7bc2-be3c-8010-8272-ef4bf7e7d6a2\" target=\"_blank\">GPT link</a>.  They left in 1985.</p>\r\n<p>I write this not to justify current American policy, which I consider a major mistake with extremely poor execution.  Rather the point is that we are pushing the Greenlanders into the arms of the Danes, when over some longer haul it could be very different.</p>\r\n<p>The FT <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.ft.com/content/ae6f0468-ccf1-45ad-806f-343f8e0b3c13\" target=\"_blank\">offers many more interesting facts about Greenland</a>, including its growing dependence on Asian foreign labor.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/01/greenland-fact-of-the-day.html\">Greenland fact of the day</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/940653626/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/940653626/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/940653626/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/940653626/marginalrevolution\"><img 